## Who each plan suits
38 employees said in the pulse survey that they have children who will need braces soon, which is why orthodontia matters.
cards
### Basic
Lowest cost at $168 a year. Suits employees with routine cleanings only and no orthodontia needs.
### Plus
$336 a year for a higher $1,500 maximum and a lower deductible. No orthodontia.
### Premier
$492 a year. A $2,500 maximum, a $25 deductible and orthodontia at 50% up to $1,500. Suits most families expecting braces.
### Family Max
$756 a year. No deductible and orthodontia up to $2,000. Pays off only for families with ongoing orthodontia.

## Recommendation
We recommend **Premier** as the default plan. It is the cheapest plan that covers orthodontia, which matters to the 38 employees whose children will need braces soon.
! Family Max costs $264 more a year than Premier and only pays off for families with ongoing orthodontia.
